    <span class="modal-close-x" onclick="closeDbScriptsModal()" title="Close">&times;</span>
    <h3>DB Scripts</h3>
    <div class="add-entry-subtitle">Review and run this entry's dbUpdates SQL scripts against a database.</div>
    <div class="meta-row-flex" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <span class="meta-live-prefix">Database: </span>
      <select id="dbScriptsTargetSelect" onchange="onDbScriptsTargetChange()"></select>
      <label style="margin-left:16px; font-size:0.85rem; font-weight:normal; display:inline-flex; align-items:center;">
        <input type="checkbox" id="dbScriptsTrialRunCheckbox" checked onclick="onDbScriptsTrialRunChange()" style="margin-right:4px;" />
        Trial run (runs for real, then rolls everything back - nothing is kept)
      </label>
    </div>
    <div id="dbScriptsLiveWarning" class="db-scripts-live-warning" style="display:none;">This database is LIVE.</div>
    <div id="dbScriptsStatus" class="field-note" style="display:none;"></div>
    <div id="dbScriptsLogLinksRow" style="margin-bottom:10px;">
      <span class="git-select-all" onclick="openPathInExplorer(DB_RUNNER_LOG_DIR, true)" title="Where every entry's DB Scripts run log lives - one file per redeploy entry, created the first time a run completes for it.">Open log folder</span><span id="dbScriptsLogLinksPipe" class="git-links-pipe" style="display:none; margin:0 6px;">|</span><span id="dbScriptsLogLink" class="git-select-all" style="display:none;" onclick="openPathInNotepad(dbRunnerLogPathForEntry(dbScriptsLogEntryDisplayNum))" title="This entry's full run output is appended here, one block per run - including trial runs and failures - and never overwritten.">View full run log...</span>
    </div>
    <div id="dbScriptsLog" class="deploy-log" style="display:none; margin-bottom:10px;"></div>
    <div id="dbScriptsGroupsContainer"></div>
    <div class="db-scripts-diff-disclaimer">
      DIFF is a point-in-time snapshot taken before a file is ever run, compared against your proposed .sql - not a live re-query of the database. Before you run it, that's effectively current vs. proposed; once run, the snapshot freezes, so DIFF goes on showing that same original before/after rather than the database's actual current state. If the database changes again afterward through some other legitimate means, DIFF won't reflect that - it'll either look like nothing changed, or show something unexpected.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

